# Archaipelago

id:landmark-ngc-7092 a oa:Landmark, oa:Place ;
    skos:altLabel "NGC 7092" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Archaipelago" ;
    oa:article <https://www.orionsarm.com/eg-article/48f8103be50fb> ;
    oa:catalogueDesignation "NGC 7092" ;
    oa:hasFictionalName true ;
    oa:note "M39, at 965 ly in Cygnus, and the Archosaurian Empire's. Cygexpa has it on the political maps and dissolved; the Archosaurians are who is there now, so both are recorded and the ring is drawn halved. The catalogue carries it as Theia_517, a Gaia-era name for the same group, with NGC 7092 among its aliases." ;
    oa:recordOrder 5 .

